---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/innerpage-common.astro";
const title =
	"Optimizely product recommendation redesign - Portfolio of Manaj Chakrobarti";
const bodyClass = "works";
import "../../styles/workspages.scss";
import Comparison from "../../layouts/components/comparison.astro";
---

<PageLayout title={title} bodyClass={bodyClass}>
	<main class="box workspage">
		<header class="inner section-header">
			<h1>
				Redesiging Optimizely's digital asset management (DAM) system
			</h1>
			<article class="project-information">
				<div class="contributions">
					<h2>My Contributions</h2>
					<ul class="no-list">
						<li>Product Design</li>
						<li>UX/UI Design</li>
						<li>Research & Testing</li>
						<li>Mobile design</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<section class="details">
					<div class="challange">
						<h2>Challenge</h2>
						<p>
							As the number of DAM users grew, finding and
							navigating assets became increasingly difficult. The
							homepage displayed assets in a flat structure,
							sorted by creation date, making folders harder to
							find as more content was added.
						</p><p>
							Users also wanted to preview folder contents without
							opening them and have a better way to discover and
							reuse assets. We wanted to create a more polished
							experience while keeping the interface familiar and
							building a foundation for future improvements.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="team">
						<h2>Team</h2>
						<p>
							I led the design effort for the DAM team, working
							with an agile team of 4–5 developers, 1 product
							manager, and 1 designer.
						</p><p>
							We collaborated closely throughout the process, with
							weekly design discussions and regular meetings
							between product managers and designers to review new
							features and dependencies.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="discover">
						<h2>Approch</h2>
						<p>
							We explored competitor products and B2C applications
							to understand different approaches to asset
							discovery and navigation.
						</p>
						<p>
							More importantly, we gathered feedback from existing
							users through interviews and worked with account
							managers and the product manager to understand their
							needs.
						</p>
						<p>
							I developed several design hypotheses around folder
							previews, asset cards, image presentation, and
							navigation. We used preference testing through
							Lyssna (formerly UsabilityHub) to validate
							individual design decisions.
						</p>
						<p>
							For the complete experience, we adapted our
							in-product NPS survey using Gainsight PX to collect
							feedback directly from our users without requiring
							them to use an external testing platform.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="solution">
						<h2>Solution</h2>
						<p>
							Based on the feedback, we designed a category-based
							homepage with improved asset presentation and
							multiple viewing options.
						</p>
						<p>
							We tested different folder views, search results,
							and asset card designs. Interestingly, users
							preferred the folder-preview approach we initially
							considered outdated. We followed their preference
							and incorporated it into the final design.
						</p>
						<p>
							The result was a redesigned homepage with Category,
							Grid, and List views.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="outcome">
						<h2>Outcome</h2>
						<p>
							The redesigned homepage provided a more intuitive
							way to discover and navigate assets. User feedback
							helped validate our design decisions and prioritize
							features for the MVP.
						</p>
						<p>
							Following the redesign, DAM usage increased
							significantly, as reflected in our product
							analytics.
						</p>

						<h2>Learning</h2>
						<p>
							I learned the importance of validating design
							assumptions rather than relying on personal
							preferences or industry conventions. Sometimes users
							value familiar patterns more than newer design
							approaches.
						</p><p>
							It also reinforced how involving users early can
							help shape a better product.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>
			</article>
		</header>

		<section class="inner before-after">
			<h2>Compare old grid view and new one</h2>
			<Comparison
				before="/images/works/opti-dam/old-home-page.png"
				after="/images/works/opti-dam/final-design-grid.png"
				beforeAlt="Image of old home page"
				afterAlt="Image of DAM home page final design"
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="inner before-after">
			<h2>Compare List View</h2>
			<Comparison
				before="/images/works/opti-dam/nc-dam-list-view-old.png"
				after="/images/works/opti-dam/opti-dam-list-view.png"
				beforeAlt="Old List View"
				afterAlt="New List View"
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="inner">
			<article class="article">
				<h2>Final Designs</h2>
				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/final-design.png"
						alt="Image of DAM home page final design"
					/>
					<figcaption>Final Design - Home View</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/final.png"
						alt="Showing the final version of rendition design"
					/>
					<figcaption>DAM Rendition</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/related.png"
						alt="Innerpage - Related Assets"
					/>
					<figcaption>Related Assets</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/versions.png"
						alt="Innerpage - Versions"
					/>
					<figcaption>Asset Versioning</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/analytics.png"
						alt="Innerpage - Asset Analytics"
					/>
					<figcaption>Asset Analytics</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/comment.png"
						alt="Innerpage - Asset Comments"
					/>
					<figcaption>Asset Comments</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/mobile.png"
						alt="NewsCred DAM Mobile Design"
					/>
					<figcaption>DAM Mobile Design</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<h2>Result of redesign</h2>
				<figure>
					<img src="/images/works/opti-dam/pendo.png" alt="Pendo" />
					<figcaption>Screenshot from Pendo</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<h2>Testing before finalize</h2>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/lyssna.png"
						alt="Image of the screenshot of usabilityhub.com tests"
					/>
					<figcaption>Screenshot of Lyssna tests</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-dam/preference-test-in-software.png"
						alt="Image of Folder Preference Test in our website via Gainsight"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Folder Preference Test in our website via Gainsight
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</article>
		</section>
	</main>
</PageLayout>
